really a tragic update to a story we  first shared on monday that little boy  who was rescued from a mobile home fire  has sadly died from his injuries amongst  their grief his family spoke with our  own victoria saha she joins us now to  share what they say happened  ryan three-year-old caiden may chum died  this morning at sunrise hospital family  and fire officials say it was all an  accident  kayden machum is described as a little  boy who loved superheroes he would run  around the house in a cape and wanted to  be the good guy his loss has dug a big  hole in a family that was already  grieving i lost the mother of my child  december 1st on her birthday  couple days later i lose my nephew and i  never would have thought this ever would  have happened ever the family was at a  candlelight vigil sunday night for the  mother of cayden's cousin my daughter  was just so tired trying to she was just  trying to help trying to focus on him  and setting up gofundme for for him  and she was so tired and so anyway when  they got home she  had what whatever she had that she was  lighting candles with at the vigil  it was sitting on her dresser  and he got it while speaking to cayden's  mom off camera she says she woke up  surrounded by flames she rushed out only  to find out caden was still inside when  they found him that he was not breathing  his mom says when she looked back on  surveillance footage kaden was mimicking  what he saw at the candlelight vigil the  night before the grief is  so hard on my daughter right now because  she thinks it's her fault  you know  she's never going to be the same  kaiden's two older sisters were at  school when the fire happened the family  has set up a gofundme that link is up on  our website brian victoria thank you for  that
 

